  "rationale": "Re-keyed to the raid-engagement build, for the same reason and with the same result as the twenty-world-year gate's baseline. raid-engagement (0.9.0) adds raid-constant.json inside contentRevision, so provenance moves from 0e63987b2823f4d991ea1c7a40944055 to 2512ea02d2a7569d8d0bacc4c5a926ca and the gate refuses to compare two builds -- correctly, since across two builds a delta is a category error rather than a regression. Nothing measured moved: a universe that never opens a portal is bit-identical before and after this change, which is itself the regression test that the engagement layer is inert at world scale. These numbers are a measurement and not a balance claim: release-plan.md forbids any balance claim before 0.5.0, and the universe they describe is still degenerate in known ways -- no god verb is exercised, no raid is initiated, and library depth stays low because the scribable list is cost-ordered so the same cheap nodes are copied repeatedly.",
